From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: cubie-a7s: count boots in RTC GP_DATA_REG7, fall back after three

A board that fails the same way on every boot is reset by the watchdog
layers straight into the same failure again. U-Boot's boot counter gives it
a way out: every U-Boot run increments the count, and once it passes
bootlimit U-Boot runs altbootcmd instead of bootcmd. The operating system
is expected to clear the counter once it has booted; a fallback boot entry
(altbootcmd) runs after three failed boots. A failure after the counter is
cleared still loops.

Where the count lives. It has to survive a warm reset. The A733 RTC keeps
eight general purpose registers while VDD_RTC is above 0.7 V (UM v0.92, RTC
GP_DATA_REGn, 0x0100 + N*4). REG7 = 0x0709011C, read on the board
on 2026-09-14: a value written before a PSCI reboot and before a WDT0
timeout reset is still there at the U-Boot prompt; after one power cycle
with 25 s off it read 0 (measured).
The vendor DT names REG7 as its boot counter (gpr_bootcount_pos = <7>) and
REG6 as its reboot flag -- a hint that the slot is meant for this, not the
reason it is used. The store follows the upstream pattern of
BOOTCOUNT_GENERIC in a register that survives a reset: i.MX8M boards in the
SNVS general purpose register (imx8mm-mx8menlo, imx8m_data_modul), i.MX6
and Vybrid boards in theirs.

Configuration, all U-Boot's own:
  * BOOTCOUNT_GENERIC (the choice default) at SYS_BOOTCOUNT_ADDR, with
    SYS_BOOTCOUNT_SINGLEWORD: magic 0xB001 in [31:16], count in [15:0]; a
    value without the magic reads as count 0. Little-endian accessors (the
    choice default).
  * BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3, as the upstream boards above.
  * altbootcmd scans only mmc_auto for extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf
    (boot_syslinux_conf), so the fallback pass does not wait on network
    targets, then restores both variables with `env default -f` and runs
    the normal scan if no card carries a fallback entry.
  * CMD_BOOTCOUNT, to read and clear the counter at the prompt.

On a board whose eMMC carries another system: U-Boot counts every run, an
interrupted autoboot included. Bring-up paths that never reach the
operating system have to clear the counter themselves; otherwise three such
runs put the next warm reset on the card's fallback entry.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
diff --git a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
index d0e7e6c59ce..a8c7c1f848b 100644
--- a/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
+++ b/configs/radxa-cubie-a7s_defconfig
@@ -80,3 +80,9 @@ CONFIG_WDT=y
 CONFIG_WDT_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_AUTOSTART=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=3
+CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_ADDR=0x0709011C
+CONFIG_SYS_BOOTCOUNT_SINGLEWORD=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_ALTBOOTCMD="setenv boot_targets mmc_auto; setenv boot_syslinux_conf extlinux/extlinux-fallback.conf; run distro_bootcmd; env default -f boot_targets boot_syslinux_conf; run distro_bootcmd"
+CONFIG_CMD_BOOTCOUNT=y
